# The safety net the devnet profiles were missing until 2026-08-09.
#
# The crank pays inline with `--and-pay`, so on the happy path this never has
# anything to do. The case it exists for is the crank dying **after** the root
# is posted and **before** the payout — which is exactly what run 4's epoch 0
# did: the co-signer was misconfigured, `crank.mjs` gave up waiting at 400s and
# exited 1, and by the time the root was posted by hand there was nothing left
# running that would ever pay it.
#
# `settle-outstanding` will not: epoch 0 was settled by then, so it is no longer
# outstanding. Without this timer the epoch stays settled-and-unpaid forever,
# and the only signal is the watchdog's `unpaid` line.
#
# CALLPOOL — pay everyone whose challenge window has closed. MAINNET clock.
#
# Separate from the crank because the challenge window is 24 hours: epoch N's
# root posts today and its money is payable tomorrow. Collapsing the two with
# `--and-pay` would hold a process open for a day.
#
#   install -m 0644 deploy/callpool-airdrop.{service,timer} /etc/systemd/system/
#   systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl enable --now callpool-airdrop.timer
#
# `--keypair` is the gas-only payer and nothing more. `claim` takes no signature
# from the recipient and the destination lives inside the merkle leaf, so this
# wallet is a submitter with no authority — which is exactly what makes
# push-based delivery safe (L8), and why a holder who distrusts us can submit
# the same instructions themselves.
#
# Unlike the crank this continues past a failure: airdrops are independent, and
# stopping early would strand money that was ready to send. A failure still
# exits non-zero, so systemd shows it and the watchdog's `unpaid` count is the
# thing that escalates.

[Unit]
Description=CALLPOOL — pay outstanding epochs (mainnet)
Documentation=https://github.com/AlphaArtrem/call-pool
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=callpool
Group=callpool
WorkingDirectory=/srv/callpool
EnvironmentFile=/etc/callpool/signer.env
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node scripts/tools/pay-outstanding.mjs \
  --keypair /etc/callpool/devnet-payer.json \
  --grace 300 --max 5

NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
PrivateDevices=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
ProtectKernelTunables=true
ProtectKernelModules=true
ProtectControlGroups=true
RestrictSUIDSGID=true
RestrictNamespaces=true
LockPersonality=true
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6
ReadWritePaths=/srv/callpool
